							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1425.msg14985#msg14985"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1425.msg14985#msg14985">Re: DON EXPANSION What a waste!!!!!!!!!</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #38 on:</b> February 23, 2005, 11:11:31 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">8 zones plus instances? It&#039;s not velious (10?) but there&#039;s certainly potential to make a very deep expansion. Sounds promising with the guild hall system as well. Neat.</div><br />The instances are in fact the same as the static zones, with part of the zone blocked off so you don&#039;t wander off too far.&nbsp; That&#039;s some cheap dungeon development!&nbsp; So yes, 8 zones.<br /><br />Velious is a much bigger expansion:<br />Iceclad Ocean<br />Eastern Wastes<br />Tower of Frozen Shadow<br />Crystal Caverns<br />Great Divide<br />Thurgadin<br />Icewell Keep<br />Kael<br />Wakening Lands<br />Siren&#039;s Grotto<br />Western Wastes<br />Dragon Necropolis<br />Temple of Veeshan<br />Sleeper&#039;s Tomb<br />Plane of Mischief<br />Plane of Growth<br /><br />Am I missing any?&nbsp; That&#039;s 16 well developed zones.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
