							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Please keep in mind that I haven&#039;t played much in the new DoN expansion but I have read many many articles on the web and talked to some folks about what they think of this.&nbsp; My feelings are mixed.&nbsp; I enjoy Ldon&#039;s ....GASP!!&nbsp; I know but they kinda are fun to do when you can&#039;t get anything together....Now if I had to do that on a regular biasis like I did when I was in my 50&#039;s it would suck LOL...&nbsp; I think this expanion was pushed out to quickly, and in my oppionion it was porked out just because EQ2 wasn&#039;t doing as well as they had hoped.&nbsp; Thinking they may get some folks to come back to EQ before they picked up a copy of &quot;the other game&quot;.&nbsp; Good from the higher ups but for those that actually play the game on a regular basis it lacks the content of other expansions we are used too.&nbsp; &nbsp;Do I like features on the new expansion oh heck yeah....The guild hall is very nice it&#039;s great to have a place where our guild can meet up and get ready for raids ect.&nbsp; Do I particularly like the new zones well we&#039;ll see im not real crazy for them what I have seen&nbsp; but who knows.&nbsp; <br /><br /> <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/soap.gif" alt="soap" border="0" />&nbsp; Now to get off that box and go back to playing :D<br /><br />/hugs<br /><br />Eshebala
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />66 Shaman<br />League of Sozobon<br />RN
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
</table>
